      "excerpt": "Zwingli began having Bible studies with a small group of students, including Conrad Grebel and Felix Manz. What they were reading was beginning to clash with what they saw around them: the Mass, infant baptism, and the church’s entanglement with civic power. Trouble was brewing as Zwingli took his case to the city council, pushing for the government’s backing of these new ideas. This led to a series of disputations, with the city council trying to decide what to do with these radical new concepts.",
