      "excerpt": "So the baptisms occurred in Zurich on January 21. But just weeks after that happened, the authorities cracked down on adult baptism, and the church had to go underground. And it was right here, right here in Zollikon, that the first church came to life. Here they met and worked out the teachings they had talked about and learned about and tried to put into practice: how they immediately wanted to start having communion, how they started sharing and baptizing. And through their preaching and their passion, a revival broke out. You can just kind of feel it, even by reading the details of how they gathered here, the radical young things that…",
