      "excerpt": "What we do know is that in 1544 he accepted a job right here in Augsburg, in current Augsburg, Germany, as the master of the waterworks of this place. These waterworks, as we can see even here in Augsburg, are still charming today. It’s a World Heritage Site. In 2019 the whole waterworks system here became a protected World Heritage Site. And that would have been a very high position. Of course, as we were talking about in Strasbourg, he would have had all that experience there and was able to bring it here. It even has in the court records how much money he received. It says he took 150 guilders a year. Looking that up in current money,…",
